algorithms.pseudocode:
Input: n×n integer matrices A, B
Output: n×n matrix C = A ⊗ B

for i = 1 to n:
  for j = 1 to n:
    C[i,j] = ∞
    for k = 1 to n:
      C[i,j] = min(C[i,j], A[i,k] + B[k,j])

Time: O(n³)
Space: O(n²)

Input: n×n public matrices A, B; target Z; bound K
Output: set of all K-bounded preimages

fiber = {}
for each n×n matrix X with entries in [-K, K]:
  if publicMap(A, B, X) == Z:
    fiber.add(X)
Return fiber

Time: O((2K+1)^(n²) · n³)
Space: O(|fiber| · n²)
